---
name: Map a Cisco ASA message to OCSF in stages
description: |
  Parses a Cisco Secure Firewall ASA message, adds the name of the firewall and
  the time from a log shipper, maps the event to OCSF, and stores the message in
  `raw_data`. Use this pipeline when you need to inspect or route the parsed
  event before mapping it.
---

from {
  received: 2026-03-05T09:20:11Z,
  firewall: "fw-north",
  message: r#"%ASA-4-106023: Deny tcp src outside:198.51.100.61/40533 dst dmz:192.0.2.69/1433 by access-group "outside_in" [0x5be21c07, 0x0]"#,
}
cisco::asa::parse message, event
event.timestamp = event.timestamp? else move received
event.hostname = event.hostname? else move firewall
cisco::asa::ocsf::map event, ocsf
this = {
  ...ocsf,
  raw_data: message,
  raw_data_size: message.length_bytes(),
}
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
